extends RefCounted
## How each new beast is painted (beast_toon.gdshader, beast_rig.gd): its line's colours, from the creature packs
## the models came from, and per stage what changes. A look:
##   col: {group: colour} for the groups body, head, arms, legs, wings, tail, horn, deco (any left out: the body's)
##   tip: {group: [colour, from, soft, to]}: the part's own colour from `from` of the way out from its joint (0..1) to
##        `to` (default 1), easing in over `soft` (hands, feet, claws, spike tips; a range near 0: where it joins)
##   belly: [colour, from, groups]: a belly patch where those parts face forward and down more than `from` (0..1)
##   stripes / bands: {group: [colour, how many]} round the part, or up it per unit of height
##   eyes: independently fitted sockets, right then left for each face. Each row holds the projected centre (u, y),
##         horizontal/vertical radii, outward view sine, near/far depth limits, mirror z, and lid intercept/slope
##         in units of the vertical radius. The last six values describe surface depth as a quadratic in normalized
##         socket coordinates: constant, u, y, u², uy, y². beast_eye_mesh.gd builds the smooth visible opening.
##   lid: the colour of an eyelid (default: the head's, darker)
##   button_eyes: solid black eyes with a glint instead of white ones with a pupil (the Draco lines)
## Per line, "base" is every stage's look and "1", "2", "3" what each stage changes.

## The frilled lizard lines (Draco, Dropo, Rocco, Floppo: the user's own design, tools/new_beasts/draco_model.py),
## one model in four elements, told apart only by the skin each element paints (skin_look): orange frills edged in
## red, a gold throat flap and brow gems, bone horns and claws, black button eyes; grown, a heavier brow.
